  "scenario_narratives": {
    "base": "Guidance delivered in FY2026, backlog converts at ~10% in FY2027, then growth fades to ~3.5% as data-center build rates normalise; adj EBITDA margin expands ~160bp to 23% on applied-systems and services mix, held back by tariffs and liquid-cooling competition.",
    "bull": "AI-factory cooling (800V DC chillers, LiquidStack liquid cooling, NVIDIA DSX reference designs) becomes a durable double-digit category through FY2029 on top of the A2L replacement cycle and electrification; margin reaches 24.5%.",
    "bear": "Hyperscaler capex digestion in 2027-28 unwinds the data-center backlog and customer advances, coinciding with a housing-driven residential slump and freight recession at Thermo King; revenue falls ~4% in FY2028 and margin reverts to ~19-20%."
  },
  "valuation_philosophy": {
    "summary": "Owner-FCF component DCF at a 9% USD WACC with SBC fully expensed and a flat diluted count. TT is a high-quality, moderately cyclical compounder whose current multiple prices in sustained double-digit growth; the house value asks what the flows support if data-center demand normalises on a normal cycle.",
    "key_risks_to_valuation": [
      "Data-center/AI capex concentration in the backlog -- a hyperscaler digestion cycle hits orders, advances and margins at once",
      "Terminal value is the majority of EV; the 18x base cap and 3% terminal growth carry most of the value",
      "Tariff cost (~$200M/yr after mitigation) and competitive entry into liquid cooling could cap the margin expansion",
      "Legacy asbestos (Aldrich/Murray) and NCI bridge items are estimates, not disclosed fair values",
      "LiquidStack consideration not closed by 2026-06-30 would reduce net cash further"
    ]
  },
